# What `gcloud run deploy --source .` UPLOADS to Cloud Build.
#
# This is not the same file as .dockerignore and gcloud does not read that one.
# .dockerignore controls what `docker build` copies once the context has arrived;
# this controls whether it is sent at all. gcloud will generate one from
# .gitignore instead -- but only inside a git repository, so do not rely on it.
#
# Build context for the VENUE image (deploy-venue.sh runs `--source .` from here).
#
# The Dockerfile beside this file copies exactly two things:
#
#     COPY requirements.txt .
#     COPY venue/ ./venue/
#
# Everything else in the repo is workshop material that has no business inside a
# container. Without this file the context is ~195MB, almost all of it .venv,
# and every deploy tars and uploads the lot before the build even starts.

# --- the big one ---------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
env/

# --- workshop material, not application code -----------------------------
agent/
solutions/
tests/
docs/
monstertix/
*.md
!requirements.txt

# --- state the workshop generates ----------------------------------------
# A rehearsal database or somebody's memory file baked into an image is a
# confusing bug the first time it wins over the real one.
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
artifacts/
memory/
.adk/

# --- secrets -------------------------------------------------------------
# .env holds the Cloud SQL password after step 10. An image layer is forever
# and anyone who can pull the image can read it.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# --- python --------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# --- vcs, editors, OS ----------------------------------------------------
.git/
.gitignore
.github/
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~

# --- assistant tooling ---------------------------------------------------
.claude/
.claude*/
CLAUDE.md
CLAUDE.local.md
.antigravity/
.antigravity*/
.cursor/
.aider*
.continue/
.windsurf/
AGENTS.md
.agent/

# --- scripts that run on a laptop, never in the image --------------------
*.sh
